        -:   31:/**
        -:   32: * Test if \a aTestPoint is on line defined by \a aSegStart and \a aSegEnd.
        -:   33: *
        -:   34: * This function is faster than #TestSegmentHit() because \a aTestPoint  should be exactly on
        -:   35: * the line.  This only works for horizontal, vertical, and 45 degree line segments.
        -:   36: *
        -:   37: * @param aSegStart The first point of the line segment.
        -:   38: * @param aSegEnd The second point of the line segment.
        -:   39: * @param aTestPoint The point to test.
        -:   40: *
        -:   41: * @return true if the point is on the line segment.
